From 0f2239314c67ff8e9ebf1f1e14a3785ac1d4d4c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:16:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: xburst2: ungate the T41 watchdog before arming it for
 reboot

jz_wdt_restart() arms the watchdog and then waits for the reset that
follows. On T41 that reset never arrives: the TCU leaves the watchdog
clock stopped, so the counter loaded by wdt_start_count() never
advances. The machine hangs in the fallback loop, printing "check
wdt." forever, and the camera has to be power-cycled.

Clear the WDT stop bit before programming the timer. wdt_stop_count()
in the same file and ingenic_wdt.c both already drive bit 16 of the
TCU stop registers for exactly this purpose.
---
 arch/mips/xburst2/soc-t41/reset.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/xburst2/soc-t41/reset.c b/arch/mips/xburst2/soc-t41/reset.c
index 05490345..2a2a4ff8 100644
--- a/arch/mips/xburst2/soc-t41/reset.c
+++ b/arch/mips/xburst2/soc-t41/reset.c
@@ -64,6 +64,15 @@ static void wdt_start_count(int msecs)
 	if(time > 65535)
 		time = 65535;
 
+	/*
+	 * Ungate the watchdog before arming it. The TCU leaves the WDT clock
+	 * stopped, so without this the counter never advances, the reset never
+	 * arrives, and jz_wdt_restart() spins printing "check wdt." forever.
+	 * wdt_stop_count() below already pokes the same bit, as does
+	 * drivers/watchdog/ingenic_wdt.c.
+	 */
+	outl(1 << 16,TCU_IOBASE + TCU_TSCR);
+
 	outl(0,WDT_IOBASE + WDT_TCER);
 
 	outl(1 << 10, WDT_IOBASE + WDT_TCSR);
